{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&nbsp;The proposed development would result in the addition of one household resulting in a maximum of 7 persons living within one half of a semi-detached dwelling. increasing the noise, disturbances and coming and goings. As such, the proposed development would significantly impact neighbouring dwellings and would be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals do not negatively impact existing neighbouring dwellings:&nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)-&nbsp;Policies D4, and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP2, and DMD1of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to comply with the required internal space standards, would result in stacked living and does not provide direct access to external amenity space for both flats. The proposal includes living spaces stacked on top of bedrooms, resulting in significant noise and disturbances to the residents. This in combination with the lack of direct access to private external amenity space for both flats and failing to reach the required internal space standards and would result in the provision of sub-standard quality of accommodation. The shared public access to private external amenity space for Flat B lacks direct access. As such, the proposed development would&nbsp;be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals provide an adequate quality level of accommodation and suitable external amenity spaces: &nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)-&nbsp; Policies D4, D6, and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policies DMNE1, DMSI 3 the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)-&nbsp;&nbsp;Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)-&nbsp;DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)",
    "The proposal fails to demonstrate compliance with the Biodiversity Net Gain Requirements and is contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.&nbsp;"
  ],
